  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Cyclone-Affected Populations in Vanuatu with Lifesaving Shelter and Non-Food Items (ES/NFI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu&#x2019;s National Disaster Management Office (NDMO) estimates that more than 110,000 people (approximately 33 per cent of the entire population of Vanuatu) were affected by Tropical Cyclone (TC) Lola which made landfall on 25 October 2023. TC Lola is the third cyclone in Vanuatu over the past 7 months and the earliest Category 5 cyclone in recorded history. With current forecasts indicating additional tropical cyclones that will impact Vanuatu in the coming months, community training and capacity building on community engagement on build back safer techniques and broad dissemination of shelter awareness materials are essential preparatory life-saving actions to mitigate threats to life, livelihood, and health.
 
IOM is working with the NDMO and partners to deliver life-saving assistance to people impacted by the cyclones. IOM is providing emergency shelter and non-food items to meet the immediate needs of people affected by TC Lola, whose homes were destroyed or damaged by the cyclone, as well as support the voluntary return of internally displaced persons. The Organization is also contributing to an evidence-based response through gathering and analyzing data on the mobility, vulnerabilities, and needs of cyclone-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
